  "response_text": "Discovering lies can be a challenging and emotionally taxing experience. It's important to take care of yourself and address the situation in a healthy way. Here are some practical steps you can take this week to help you move forward:\n\n1. Take a break: Give yourself some time to process the information and emotions you're feeling. Take a break from social media and news outlets that may be triggering your emotions.\n\n2. Seek support: Reach out to friends, family, or a trusted professional for support. Talking about your feelings with someone you trust can help you feel less alone and more understood.\n\n3. Set boundaries: If you feel uncomfortable or unsafe in your current situation, set boundaries with the person who lied to you. This may involve distancing yourself from them or seeking a new relationship.\n\n4. Practice self-care: Take care of your physical and emotional well-being by getting enough sleep, eating well, and engaging in activities that bring you joy.\n\n5. Consider seeking professional help: If your trust issues are impacting your daily life, consider seeking help from a therapist or counselor. They can provide you with tools and strategies to help you rebuild trust and move forward.\n\nRemember, it's okay to take things one step at a time and to seek help when you need it. Trust takes time to rebuild, and it's important to be patient and compassionate with yourself throughout the process.",
